# An allowlist, not a denylist: everything is excluded, and only what the Go
# service images build from is let back in.
#
# The build context is the repository root, because a service image needs its
# own module and the shared packages beside it. A denylist would have to keep up
# with every new directory — and the one that matters is .env, which holds API
# tokens. Excluding by default means a secret can never be baked into an image
# by someone forgetting to list it here.
*

!apps/cortex
!apps/nexus
!apps/siphon
!packages/common
!packages/contracts

# Tests are not built into an image, and fixtures can be large.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
